        43.65,
        43.81,
        44.19,
        44.37,
        44.63,
        44.83,
        45.01,
        45.21,
        45.31,
        45.55,
        45.69,
        46.09
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "lyric-011-8886fbbf",
      "text": "It is perfectly appropriate to share my email address to subscribe to a newsletter, but it\u2019s wholly inappropriate to send them my calendar too.",
      "start": 47.01,
      "end": 53.15,
      "words": [
        47.01,
        47.43,
        47.55,
        47.89,
        48.33,
        48.57,
        48.77,
        48.91,
        49.13,
        49.47,
        49.63,
        49.95,
        50.15,
        50.27,
        50.59,
        50.97,
        51.05,
        51.13,
        51.41,
        51.63,
        51.99,
        52.23,
        52.33,
        52.47,
        52.85,
        53.15
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "lyric-012-fc60f0df",
      "text": "It turns out I\u2019m not the first person to think of this, and at the time of writing Google Scholar surfaces ~250k results if you search \u201ccontextual integrity artificial intelligence.\u201d In essence, what you can share depends heavily on why you\u2019re sharing it and who you\u2019re sharing it to.",
      "start": 54.15,
      "end": 69.91,
      "words": [
        54.15,
        54.576,
        54.744,
        54.919,
        55.002,
        55.089,
        55.202,
        55.353,
        55.55,
        55.772,
        55.904,
        56.041,
        56.184,
        56.53,
        56.898,
        57.048,
        57.188,
        57.328,
        57.481,
        57.852,
        58.355,
        58.874,
        59.308,
        59.954,
        60.972,
        61.396,
        61.65,
        61.759,
        62.055,
        62.904,
        63.538,
        64.045,
        64.887,
        65.875,
        66.222,
        66.645,
        66.748,
        66.903,
        67.122,
        67.52,
        67.928,
        68.145,
        68.261,
        68.313,
        68.538,
        68.747,
        68.944,
        69.119,
        69.209,
        69.282,
        69.548,
        69.705,
        69.91
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "lyric-013-af36f948",
      "text": "There are a lot of approaches to solving this problem for LLMs (Hassanpour & Yang, 2026), but my options narrow significantly once I embrace the following constraints:",
      "start": 70.65,
      "end": 77.75,
      "words": [
        70.65,
        71.004,
        71.204,
        71.381,
        71.633,
        71.9,
        72.142,
        72.4,
        72.63,
        72.86,
        73.005,
        73.249,
        73.453,
        73.79,
        74.227,
        74.548,
        74.705,
        75.022,
        75.305,
        75.992,
        76.33,
        76.491,
        76.67,
        76.872,
        77.055,
        77.325,
        77.75
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "lyric-014-0a144184",
      "text": "I can\u2019t out-prompt prompt-injection (Abdelnabi & Bagdasarian, 2026)",
      "start": 78.77,
      "end": 82.53,
      "words": [
        78.77,
        78.946,
        79.434,
        79.85,
        80.082,
        80.29,
        80.514,
        80.738,
        80.986,
        81.458,
        82.53
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "lyric-015-a7657ec7",
      "text": "The agent needs private information to be useful",
      "start": 83.13,
      "end": 85.37,
      "words": [
        83.13,
        83.19,
        83.49,
        84.03,
        84.31,
        84.75,
        84.99,
        85.07,
        85.37
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "lyric-016-15ed7ba3",
      "text": "Private information can be rephrased (\u201dKevin\u2019s date\u201d \u2192 \u201cKevin\u2019s romantic encounter\u201d)",
      "start": 87.15,
      "end": 91.85,
      "words": [
        87.15,
        87.62,
        88.103,
        88.45,
        88.903,
        89.648,
        89.99,
        90.17,
        90.47,
        90.865,
        91.32,
        91.45,
        91.85
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "lyric-017-61f49b3f",
      "text": "Checks need to be fast and ideally not make more LLM calls",
      "start": 94.03,
      "end": 97.35,
      "words": [
        94.03,
        94.13,
        94.33,
        94.45,
        94.57,
        94.99,
        95.29,
        95.63,
        95.99,
        96.33,
        96.59,
        97.05,
        97.35
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "lyric-018-a52e4e40",
      "text": "It needs to work but not be overly annoying",
      "start": 99.09,
      "end": 100.85,
      "words": [
        99.09,
        99.15,
        99.27,
        99.41,
        99.71,
        99.91,
        100.07,
        100.21,
        100.49,
        100.85
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "lyric-019-a2c74a84",
      "text": "I am not an AI security researcher",
      "start": 102.55,
      "end": 104.37,
      "words": [
        102.55,
        102.75,
        102.87,
        103.05,
        103.21,
        103.37,
        103.69,
        104.37
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "lyric-020-65a1a30c",
      "text": "But I do care about my privacy.",
      "start": 105.21,
      "end": 106.61,
      "words": [
        105.21,
        105.49,
        105.59,
        105.73,
        105.97,
        106.09,
        106.23,
        106.61
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "lyric-021-2f516e63",
      "text": "And I really want to use my agent.",
      "start": 107.41,
      "end": 108.87,
      "words": [
        107.41,
        107.59,
        107.71,
        107.93,
        108.09,
        108.23,
        108.39,
        108.53,
        108.87
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "lyric-022-2dab67ed",
      "text": "Defining Boundaries",
      "start": null,
      "end": null
    },
    {
      "id": "lyric-023-0db8e382",
      "text": "Agent harnesses are fundamentally pretty simple: The user sends the agent a message, the agent thinks about it, it potentially executes some actions via tool calls, and then it responds back to the user with an answer.",
      "start": 111.03,
      "end": 123.09,
      "words": [
        111.03,
        111.57,
        112.09,
        112.21,
        112.65,
        113.23,
        113.59,
        114.35,
        114.55,
        114.85,
        115.07,
        115.27,
        115.41,
        115.67,
        116.19,
        116.43,
        116.75,
        117.05,
        117.27,
        117.81,
        118.47,
        119.17,
        119.39,
        119.67,
        119.93,
        120.19,
        120.51,
        121.13,
        121.27,
        121.37,
        121.69,
        122.01,
        122.19,
        122.25,
        122.45,
        122.67,
        122.79,
        123.09
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "lyric-025-014d2c60",
      "text": "If we assume the agent is allowed to read private information (otherwise it\u2019s not a particularly useful agent), the trust boundary then exists between the agent and the tools it calls since that\u2019s the only way information can come in or out of the system.",
      "start": 123.95,
      "end": 136.71,
      "words": [
        123.95,
        124.25,
        124.37,
        124.69,
        124.87,
        125.13,
        125.31,
        125.59,
        125.79,
        125.95,
        126.23,
        126.79,
        127.45,
        127.61,
        127.77,
        127.89,
        128.07,
        128.43,
        128.91,
        129.29,
        130.35,
        130.69,
        131.05,
        131.29,
        131.61,
        132.01,
        132.17,
        132.45,
        132.67,
        132.77,
        133.07,
        133.23,
        133.57,
        134.01,
        134.17,
        134.33,
        134.41,
        134.61,
        134.75,
        135.13,
        135.47,
        135.63,
        135.85,
        135.99,
        136.19,
        136.29,
        136.39,
        136.71
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "lyric-026-0390334f",
      "text": "In an ideal world we simply tell the agent \u201chey be careful about sharing private information\u201d (and indeed most agents do this by default) but agents are both vulnerable to prompt injection and their own internal reasoning, particularly as context grows.",
      "start": 137.41,
      "end": 150.37,
      "words": [
        137.41,
        137.93,
        138.05,
        138.25,
        138.59,
        138.77,
        139.03,
        139.29,
        139.41,
        139.67,
        140.03,
        140.45,
        140.81,
        141.03,
        141.25,
        141.53,
        142.03,
        142.57,
        142.77,
        142.97,
        143.23,
        143.41,
        143.51,
        143.65,
        144.01,
        144.83,
        145.31,
        145.51,
        145.69,
        146.01,
        146.25,
        146.51,
        146.77,
        147.23,
        147.39,
        147.55,
        147.87,
        148.27,
        149.25,
        149.61,
        149.93,
        150.37
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "lyric-027-2fea2887",
      "text": "Hence this becomes an egress problem; we must set up a checkpoint between the agent and its tools.",
      "start": 151.21,
      "end": 156.35,
      "words": [
        151.21,
        151.49,
        151.91,
        152.25,
        152.43,
        152.69,
        153.09,
        153.61,
        153.83,
        154.19,
        154.29,
        154.43,
        154.73,
        155.15,
        155.33,
        155.61,
        155.89,
        156.03,
        156.35
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "lyric-029-a07745ac",
      "text": "Now, when an agent talks to a tool (e.g. load your calendar, fill out a form), the checkpoint must do two things:",
      "start": 157.57,
      "end": 164.11,
      "words": [
        157.57,
        157.93,
        158.33,
        158.45,
        158.61,
        158.93,
        159.13,
        159.23,
        159.47,
        159.83,
        160.13,
        160.43,
        160.57,
        160.95,
        161.35,
        161.53,
        161.65,
        161.93,
        162.63,
        162.97,
        163.25,
        163.49,
        163.71,
        164.11
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "lyric-030-72c0d6e4",
      "text": "Determine if we\u2019re reading private information (ingress)",
      "start": 165.41,
      "end": 167.77,
      "words": [
        165.41,
        165.61,
        165.87,
        165.92,
        165.97,
        166.17,
        166.49,
        166.97,
        167.77
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "lyric-031-ac321fd9",
      "text": "Determine if we\u2019re potentially sending private information (egress)",
      "start": 169.79,
      "end": 172.47,
      "words": [
        169.79,
        169.79,
        169.97,
        170.02,
        170.07,
        170.45,
        171.01,
        171.35,
        171.85,
        172.47
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "lyric-032-54a93409",
      "text": "These aren\u2019t independent; once private information is read into the LLM context, every single future tool call becomes a potential data leak.",
      "start": 173.43,
      "end": 181.19,
      "words": [
        173.43,
        173.81,
        173.95,
        174.09,
        174.51,
        175.39,
        175.79,
        176.13,
        176.45,
        176.65,
        176.87,
        176.99,
        177.43,
        177.77,
        178.65,
        178.97,
        179.25,
        179.55,
        179.77,
        180.13,
        180.35,
        180.61,
        180.87,
        181.19
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "lyric-033-852520eb",
      "text": "Information Flow",
      "start": null,
      "end": null
    },
    {
      "id": "lyric-034-614a7ed0",
      "text": "Ingress Classification",
      "start": null,
      "end": null
    },
    {
      "id": "lyric-035-2bc262fe",
      "text": "But how do we determine what\u2019s private?",
      "start": 182.43,
      "end": 184.57,
      "words": [
        182.43,
        183.07,
        183.53,
        183.65,
        183.71,
        184.03,
        184.17,
        184.31,
        184.57
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "lyric-036-8e57a736",
      "text": "That question alone is worthy of a philosophy class, but in practical terms we can assume that private information comes from private data sources - if you can find it on Wikipedia, it\u2019s probably not very private.",
      "start": 185.29,
      "end": 196.49,
      "words": [
        185.29,
        185.61,
        185.89,
        186.17,
        186.39,
        186.65,
        186.81,
        186.89,
        187.29,
        187.73,
        188.01,
        188.35,
        188.73,
        189.07,
        189.29,
        189.43,
        189.83,
        190.03,
        190.39,
        190.81,
        191.33,
        191.57,
        191.91,
        192.13,
        192.49,
        193.41,
        193.49,
        193.59,
        193.87,
        193.99,
        194.09,
        194.33,
        195.03,
        195.13,
        195.63,
        195.91,
        196.15,
        196.49
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "lyric-037-63e037b7",
      "text": "The hard part is determining what sources contain private information; the conservative approach is to assume information is private by default and only relax that assumption if we\u2019re certain otherwise (e.g. a tool that returns the current time).",
      "start": 197.24,
      "end": 210.41,
      "words": [
        197.24,
        197.49,
        197.81,
        198.05,
        198.27,
        198.65,
        198.99,
        199.35,
        199.89,
        200.25,
        200.73,
        201.51,
        201.95,
        202.39,
        202.73,
        202.85,
        203.17,
        203.57,
        203.77,
        204.07,
        204.27,
        204.65,
        205.07,
        205.47,
        205.85,
        206.05,
        206.37,
        206.65,
        206.7,
        206.75,
        207.25,
        207.79,
        208.61,
        208.89,
        209.11,
        209.23,
        209.37,
        209.71,
        209.85,
        210.03,
        210.41
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "lyric-039-e4664da6",
      "text": "Egress Classification",
      "start": null,
      "end": null
    },
    {
      "id": "lyric-040-40d6f3ba",
      "text": "On the other side we need to determine when it\u2019s okay to share; on a practical level that means allowing or denying agent tool calls.",
      "start": 212.03,
      "end": 218.71,
      "words": [
        212.03,
        212.53,
        212.65,
        212.77,
        213.03,
        213.23,
        213.35,
        213.45,
        213.79,
        214.01,
        214.1,
        214.19,
        214.43,
        214.63,
        214.79,
        215.31,
        215.43,
        215.75,
        216.15,
        216.43,
        216.67,
        217.17,
        217.39,
        217.71,
        218.13,
        218.43,
        218.71
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "lyric-041-732f0afc",
      "text": "If the agent has not read any private information yet then this is simple - allow the tool call.",
      "start": 219.35,
      "end": 223.53,
      "words": [
        219.35,
        219.49,
        219.61,
